# Firewall Configuration

## Enable Required Ports

```bash
sudo ufw allow 22/tcp
sudo ufw allow 443/tcp
sudo ufw allow 1514/tcp
sudo ufw allow 1515/tcp
sudo ufw reload
```

## Verify Rules

```bash
sudo ufw status
```

---

# Why Port 22 Was Allowed

Port 22 is used for SSH remote administration.

Without allowing port 22:

* SSH access would fail
* Remote administration would be impossible
* The administrator could lock themselves out of the server

Although the Wazuh installer did not explicitly warn about port 22, it is required for Linux server management.

